            "url": "{{baseUrl}}/api/marketing/campaigns/send-bulk",
            "body": {
              "mode": "formdata",
              "formdata": [
                {
                  "key": "campaignName",
                  "value": "Q4 Financial Services ABM Outreach",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "targetDomain",
                  "value": "{{contactDomain}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "subject",
                  "value": "A practical path to faster exception settlement at {{company}}",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "contentHtml",
                  "value": "<p>Hi {{firstName}},</p>\n<p>Financial services organizations are under growing pressure to make settlement faster, strengthen operational resilience, and provide clear oversight across complex workflows. Many teams still rely on manual document handling and disconnected processes, which can slow exception resolution and make it harder to identify the source of delays.</p>\n<p>Our enterprise platform helps connect ERP workflows with AI-assisted document processing and operational integrations. It can capture and classify incoming documents, extract key information, validate it against business rules, and route exceptions to the right people for review. Teams retain control over approval steps while reducing repetitive data entry and handoffs.</p>\n<p>For {{company}}, a practical modernization effort could begin with one high-volume settlement or supply chain workflow. We would map the current process, identify where data is re-entered or exceptions wait, and outline a phased integration approach that works with your existing ERP and security requirements.</p>\n<p>The initial architecture review can cover:</p>\n<ul><li>Current ERP and document-processing touchpoints</li><li>Exception queues, approval controls, and audit requirements</li><li>Integration options and a focused pilot scope</li><li>Measures for processing time, exception rates, and operational visibility</li></ul>\n<p>If useful, I can send a short solution brief and walk through a reference architecture with your engineering and operations stakeholders.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://example.com/schedule\">Schedule a 15-minute Architecture Review</a>, or reply with a time that works for you.</p>\n<p>Best regards,<br>{{senderName}}<br>Agentic AI Platform</p>\n<p><small>If this topic is not relevant to your role, reply and we will update your contact preferences.</small></p>",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "fromEmail",
                  "value": "{{senderEmail}}",
                  "type": "text",
                  "description": "Must match the verified SMTP_FROM configured on the server."
                },
                {
                  "key": "senderName",
                  "value": "Agentic AI Platform",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "replyTo",
                  "value": "sales@example.com",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "variables",
                  "value": "firstName",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "variables",
                  "value": "company",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "variables",
                  "value": "senderName",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "key": "attachment",
                  "type": "file",
                  "src": ""
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "SMTP bulk email endpoint. Use multipart/form-data. Provide all text fields and optionally select one attachment file (max 10 MiB). Server must have SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USERNAME, SMTP_PASSWORD and SMTP_FROM configured. Enter fromEmail in the request form; it must equal the verified SMTP_FROM server setting."
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Campaign request accepted', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(202); });",
